{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>From inside and from outside you shall overlay it.</b> Betzalel made three arks — two of gold and one of wood. Four walls and a bottom for each, and open at the top. He placed the wooden one inside the gold one, and [another] gold one inside the wooden one, and covered its upper rim with gold. Thus it was overlaid from inside and from outside (Yoma 72b)." "<b>A crown of gold.</b> A kind of crown encircling it all around, above its rim — for he made the outer ark higher than the inner one, so that it rose to the thickness of the cover and a bit above it. And when the cover rests upon the thickness of the walls, the crown rises above all the thickness of the cover ever so slightly, and it is a sign for the crown of Torah."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:26.186851584Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}